<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Thorpe returns three weeks after his preventive visit, about four months after his lip surgery. He has done 30 of his 36 cardiac rehabilitation sessions and has had no angina. His low-dose CT of the chest showed a 4 mm smooth nodule in the right lower lobe, read as benign-appearing (Lung-RADS category 2), and coronary artery calcification, as expected with his heart disease. The stool immunochemical test was negative, and his HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B tests were negative. He registered with the urban Indian health program near his home and had his first dental check-up there last week; the dentist found no problems in his mouth. He has no new lip or mouth sores and no neck lumps. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cardiac rehabilitation</td><td>30 of 36 sessions; no angina</td></tr><tr><td>Low-dose chest CT</td><td>4 mm benign-appearing nodule (Lung-RADS 2); coronary calcification</td></tr><tr><td>Other results</td><td>Stool test, HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B negative</td></tr><tr><td>Dental check-up</td><td>Done through the urban Indian health program; normal</td></tr><tr><td>Lip</td><td>No new sore; no neck lumps</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
