<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Squamous cell carcinoma of the left lower lip, excised (C00.1)</content>. No recurrence about four months after excision; dental check-up normal. [S]<list><item>Lip, mouth and neck examination every 1 to 3 months for the rest of the first year.</item><item>Continue sun protection.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic coronary disease with stable angina (I25.119)</content>. No angina; blood pressure 122/76; LDL at goal last month. Coronary calcification on the screening CT is expected and does not change treatment. [S]<list><item>Continue current medicines.</item><item>Finish rehabilitation, then exercise at home or at the community gym most days.</item><item>Review every 4 to 6 months.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Actinic keratoses (L57.0)</content>. Two lesions on the backs of the hands treated with cryotherapy. [S]<list><item>Blistering and crusting expected for one to two weeks.</item><item>Recheck at the next visit; biopsy any lesion that does not clear.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Examination of the lips, mouth, and neck</td><td>Every 1 to 3 months in year 1, 2 to 6 months in year 2, 4 to 8 months in years 3 to 5, then yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No recurrence or new lesion; no neck nodes</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Imaging of the primary site and neck</td><td>Before treatment as indicated; afterwards only for symptoms or findings</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No symptoms or findings</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Low-dose CT of the chest (second primary and lung cancer screening)</td><td>Yearly for eligible former smokers</td><td>Completed today</td><td>4 mm benign-appearing nodule, Lung-RADS 2; next screening CT in one year</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Sun protection of the lips and skin</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Daily lip balm with sunscreen and a hat</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Tobacco and alcohol use</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tobacco-free; AUDIT-C 2 at the preventive visit</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Dental evaluation</td><td>After diagnosis, then routine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>First check-up last week through the urban Indian health program, at his choice; normal</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure (goal below 130/80)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>122/76, at goal</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight, BMI, and physical activity</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>91.0 kg, BMI 26.6, down 3 kg since June</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Angina frequency and nitroglycerin use</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adherence and side effects: aspirin, high-intensity statin, beta-blocker</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>All taken daily; no side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lipid panel</td><td>4 to 12 weeks after starting or changing lipid therapy, then every 3 to 12 months; goal LDL below 55 mg/dL</td><td>Up to date</td><td>LDL 51 mg/dL five weeks ago; next in 6 to 12 months</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Cardiac rehabilitation</td><td>After a heart attack or for stable angina: up to 36 sessions</td><td>Completed today</td><td>30 of 36 sessions</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression screen (PHQ-2 or PHQ-9)</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PHQ-2 0 at the preventive visit</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Influenza and COVID-19 vaccination review</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Influenza vaccine given at the preventive visit; Tdap given today; COVID-19 vaccine declined for now</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Lip cancer removed with clear margins and no recurrence on surveillance through four months. Outcome by 1951-10-26: Excised with clear margins; no recurrence or neck nodes at four months [S]</item><item>LDL cholesterol below 55 mg/dL on secondary prevention. Outcome by 1951-09-21: LDL 51 mg/dL on atorvastatin 80 mg and ezetimibe 10 mg [S]</item><item>Blood pressure below 130/80 mmHg. Outcome by 1951-09-21: 124/76 on metoprolol [S]</item><item>Complete cardiac rehabilitation and walk uphill without angina. Outcome by 1951-10-26: 30 of 36 sessions done; no angina and no nitroglycerin use for two months [S]</item><item>Stay tobacco-free and protect his lips and skin from the sun. Outcome by 1951-10-26: Tobacco-free; lip balm with sunscreen and a hat used daily [S]</item></list><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Tdap vaccine [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Head and Neck Cancers (cancer of the lip and oral cavity) (2026); 2023 AHA/ACC/ACCP/ASPC/NLA/PCNA Guideline for the Management of Patients With Chronic Coronary Disease (2023); 2018 AHA/ACC/AACVPR/AAPA/ABC/ACPM/ADA/AGS/APhA/ASPC/NLA/PCNA Guideline on the Management of Blood Cholesterol (2018); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, ischemic heart disease monograph (2026); Lung Cancer: Screening (2021); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Lip surveillance and coronary disease review in two to three months. Second zoster vaccine dose then. Low-dose CT and stool test in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
